# COM: Run `coverage candidate-test` WITHOUT -j so the default job count
# COM: (os.cpu_count()) drives parallel execution. With 3 input files and
# COM: len(TEST_FLAGS)=4 flag variants each, all 12 executions must complete
# COM: and none be skipped.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/candidate_tests
# RUN: %coverage candidate-test --output-dir %t/candidate_tests --instrumented-bin "$(dirname %sancov-llc)" --candidate-tests-dir %S/fixtures/new-tests-parallel --n 3 | tee %t/candidate_tests.log

# COM: Final progress line reports the tallies across all flag runs.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/candidate_tests.log --check-prefix=EXEC
# EXEC: complete=12  skipped=0  remaining=0

# COM: Each of the 12 successful runs must leave exactly one sancov file, so the
# COM: total number of sancov files across all test dirs must be exactly 12.
# RUN: find %t/candidate_tests -name '*.sancov' | wc -l | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SANCOV_COUNT
# SANCOV_COUNT: 12
